<title>USA: Allegheny Teledyne CEO Rutledge resigns.</title>
<headline>Allegheny Teledyne CEO Rutledge resigns.</headline>
<dateline>PITTSBURGH 1997-02-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Allegheny Teledyne Inc said Wednesday its president and chief executive officer, William Rutledge, has resigned, citing personal and family reasons.</p>
<p>The company said its chairman Richard Simmons will serve as president and chief executive officer of the company. During the transition, Rutledge will be available to assist Simmons with respect to Allegeny Teledyne's metals businesses.</p>
</text>
